# Block Registry & Registration

## The registry is the only source of block behavior

- `BlockDefinition` = `{ type, label, icon, category, isContainer?,
  canAcceptChild?, defaultProps, propsSchema, render, ContentFields,
  source: 'core' | 'tenant' | 'plugin', capabilities? }`.
- Consumers (canvas, DnD, inspector) are dispatcher-only. Never write
  `if (block.type === 'heading') { ... } else if (...)` anywhere outside
  the registry lookup itself.
- `Block.type` validation is a LIVE registry `.refine()`, not a frozen
  static enum. New types must be addable without editing a giant switch or
  union type elsewhere in the codebase.

## Two registration models — nothing else is allowed

**Model A — client-bundled (default, safe path for real render logic)**
- Host/plugin imports a module and calls `registerBlock(definition)`
  BEFORE `<PageBuilder>` mounts.
- `type` MUST be namespaced: `tenant:…` or `plugin:vendor.block`. Never
  allow a plugin/tenant type to collide with a core primitive name
  (`heading`, `box`, `text`, etc.) — this is a `blockRegistrationGuard`
  error, not a silent override.
- `render`, `ContentFields`, and `propsSchema` all ship in the same bundle.

**Model B — server-defined, data-driven (no new render code)**
- Tenant JSON spec = `propsSchema` + a composition tree of EXISTING
  primitives only, fetched via `fetchDynamicBlocks`.
- Field specs use `{ key, kind, options?, translatable? }` where `kind` is
  drawn from the SAME enum documented in
  `docs/page-builder/api/field-types.md`. An unknown `kind` at
  registration time is a `blockRegistrationGuard` ERROR — never a silent
  fallback to a plain-text field.
- The mapping from `kind` → actual inspector control lives ONLY in
  `fieldAdapterResolve.ts`. Do not hand-roll a second mapping anywhere else
  (e.g. inline in a Model B loader). Any new `kind` requires updating
  `fieldAdapterResolve.ts` AND the doc page in the same change.

**Absolutely forbidden, no exceptions:**
- `eval()` or `new Function()` of any fetched/remote code as a block
  `render`.
- Any "trusted partner" exception that skips the sandbox or the Model A/B
  distinction.
- Signed dynamic `import()` of remote render bundles — this is Phase 19,
  explicitly NOT v1. Do not implement it unless specifically asked to work
  on that phase.

## Registration lifecycle

- Duplicate `type` on `registerBlock` → loud error. Never silently
  override an existing registration.
- Namespace violation → rejected by `blockRegistrationGuard`.
- Removing a plugin must not crash existing pages that reference its
  block type.
- Unknown `type` encountered at render time → `fallbackBlock`: a
  tree-preserving placeholder ("Unavailable block: <type>"). Never throw,
  never drop the node's data. Must render identically (same fallback UI)
  across canvas, preview, and Open Page.
- Definition version bumps migrate instance data via `schemaVersion` /
  per-type migration; otherwise instances render via fallback until
  migrated — never silently coerced into a mismatched shape.

## Capability gating

`allowRegisterPluginBlocks` gates Model A registration in a workspace.
`allowDynamicBlockDefs` gates Model B. Both come from host-injected
`capabilities` (ADR-05) — the engine hides registration entry points when
false, but this is NOT sufficient on its own; the host must also re-check
server-side before persisting anything that references a gated type.
